<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Two Twitch factions, added to the SAVE-SAFE mod (this one is save="0").

  Why this is save-compatible: a faction is a definition loaded fresh at every
  game start/load, and these two own NO territory and NO god-seeded stations
  (which only place on a NEW game). Their ships come purely from our MD spawns,
  so they light up on an existing save without a new playthrough.

    twitchally  -> starts allied (+1) with the player and every other faction
                   except xenon/khaak. Relations are UNLOCKED, so they drift and
                   can be negotiated like a normal faction's.
    twitchfoe   -> at war with the player, with twitchally, and with every
                   other faction in the game (relation -1, locked)

  VISIBILITY: these used to carry tags="hidden", which is the tag vanilla puts
  on its non-entity factions (civilian / criminal / outlaw / smuggler / visitor /
  ownerless / holyorderfanatic). The engine strips hidden factions out of
  GetLibrary("factions"), which is the single source both the Encyclopedia
  (ui/addons/ego_detailmonitor/menu_encyclopedia.lua:792) and the Diplomacy menu
  (menu_diplomacy.lua:1188) enumerate — so they had no encyclopedia entry at all.
  Dropped it from both. twitchfoe then mirrors how khaak/xenon stay
  visible-but-untouchable:

    nodiplomacyselection  -> cannot be picked as a diplomacy target
    <relations locked="1">-> relations can never drift or be negotiated

  twitchally gets neither of those, so its relations behave normally.

  twitchfoe keeps notradeoffer/noresupply/privateloadout/privateship — it owns
  nothing tradeable, so there is nothing to trade at, resupply from, or buy.
  twitchally NO LONGER has them: chat can build twitchally stations (`!buy wharf`),
  and those tags would leave a working wharf with an empty shelf. See the note on
  the faction itself.

  Deliberately NOT using the `aggressive` tag: only khaak has it and only with
  behaviourset="khaak"; no script reads it, so it is engine behaviour we can't
  inspect. Relation -1 to everything already makes twitchfoe universally hostile.

  Reusing existing colours / icons / diplomacy banners (faction_argon,
  faction_xenon) so no new art is needed. Structure and the exhaustive relation
  list are copied from the vanilla khaak/xenon entries in libraries/factions.xml.

  DLC faction ids (boron, terran/pioneers/yaki, split/freesplit/fallensplit/court,
  loanshark/scavenger, kaori) are listed unconditionally. That is safe and is what
  Egosoft itself does: ego_dlc_boron's factions.xml references Terran, Split and
  Pirate factions while depending on those DLCs only with optional="true" (which
  merely fixes load order). Relations to factions that aren't installed are ignored.
-->
<diff>
  <add sel="/factions">
    <faction id="twitchally" name="{90042,1}" description="{90042,2}" shortname="{90042,3}"
             prefixname="{90042,4}" spacename="{90042,5}" homespacename="{90042,6}"
             primaryrace="argon" behaviourset="default">
      <!-- NO inert-faction tags. twitchally used to carry
           `noresupply notradeoffer privateloadout privateship`, which was correct
           while it owned nothing: those tags are what vanilla puts on factions that
           exist only as a relation target, and they mean "makes no trade offers,
           resupplies nobody, sells the player none of its ships or loadouts".
           Chat can now BUILD twitchally stations (a wharf, a trading station, an
           equipment dock), and every one of those tags would make the station a
           decoration: docked but no trades, no restock, nothing on the shelf. The
           tags go, so an ally station behaves like any other faction's. -->
      <color ref="faction_argon" />
      <!-- Working capital. The equipment traders in libraries/jobs.xml BUY their
           cargo before they can deliver it, and a faction with an empty account
           cannot fill a single station shelf. Vanilla only writes <account> on the
           player (NPC balances are otherwise engine-managed), so this is belt and
           braces — harmless if the engine already funds the faction, and the
           difference between a working dock and an empty one if it does not.
           Must sit between <color> and <icon>: factions.xsd fixes the child order. -->
      <account amount="50000000" />
      <icon active="faction_argon" inactive="faction_argon" banner="diplomacy_banner_argon" />
      <!-- LICENCES TO BUY. Equipment and ship wares carry
           `<restriction licence="generaluseequipment|militaryequipment|generaluseship|
           capitalship|capitalequipment">`, and a faction can only sell a restricted
           ware to someone holding a licence of that type ISSUED BY THAT FACTION.
           twitchally had no <licences> block at all, so it could not issue one, and
           nothing on its shelves could ever be bought.

           Every vanilla faction that owns a tradeable station has this block; the
           ones without it (civilian, criminal, outlaw, smuggler, xenon, khaak) are
           precisely the ones that sell nothing.

           `minrelation` is what the player must reach to hold the licence.
           twitchally starts at +1 with the player (see <relations> below), so these
           are all granted on sight — no ceremony chain, deliberately: these docks
           are a gift from chat, not a reputation grind. Names come from this mod's
           own text page 90042, so nothing borrows an Argon licence's wording.
           Ordering is fixed by factions.xsd: color, account, icon, licences,
           relations. -->
      <licences>
        <licence type="generaluseequipment" name="{90042,21}" description="{90042,22}"
                 minrelation="-0.01" tags="basic" />
        <licence type="generaluseship" name="{90042,25}" description="{90042,26}"
                 minrelation="-0.01" tags="basic" />
        <licence type="militaryequipment" name="{90042,23}" description="{90042,24}"
                 minrelation="-0.01" />
        <licence type="capitalequipment" name="{90042,27}" description="{90042,28}"
                 minrelation="-0.01" />
      </licences>
      <!-- Starts allied (+1) with the player and the whole galaxy, and unlike
           twitchfoe the block is NOT locked and the faction is NOT
           nodiplomacyselection: relations drift from combat/diplomacy like any
           normal faction, and it can be picked as a diplomacy target.
           Two deliberate exceptions to "allied with everyone":
             xenon / khaak -> -1. They are hostile to all life in X4 and their own
               relation blocks are locked, so an ally that ignored them would just
               look broken escorting the player through a Xenon sector.
             twitchfoe     -> not listed here on purpose. twitchfoe's own
               <relations locked="1"> already pins the pair at -1; declaring the
               same pair twice with a different lock state is ambiguous. -->
      <relations>
        <relation faction="player" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="alliance" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="antigone" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="argon" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="buccaneers" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="civilian" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="criminal" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="hatikvah" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="holyorder" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="holyorderfanatic" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="ministry" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="outlaw" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="paranid" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="scaleplate" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="smuggler" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="teladi" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="trinity" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="visitor" relation="1" />
        <!-- Kingdom End -->
        <relation faction="boron" relation="1" />
        <!-- Cradle of Humanity -->
        <relation faction="terran" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="pioneers" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="yaki" relation="1" />
        <!-- Split Vendetta -->
        <relation faction="split" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="freesplit" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="fallensplit" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="court" relation="1" />
        <!-- Tides of Avarice -->
        <relation faction="loanshark" relation="1" />
        <relation faction="scavenger" relation="1" />
        <!-- Timelines -->
        <relation faction="kaori" relation="1" />
        <!-- Permanently hostile to all life; see note above. -->
        <relation faction="xenon" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="khaak" relation="-1" />
      </relations>
    </faction>
    <faction id="twitchfoe" name="{90042,11}" description="{90042,12}" shortname="{90042,13}"
             prefixname="{90042,14}" spacename="{90042,15}" homespacename="{90042,16}"
             primaryrace="argon" behaviourset="default"
             tags="nobuildunits nodiplomacyselection noresupply notradeoffer privateloadout privateship">
      <color ref="faction_xenon" />
      <icon active="faction_xenon" inactive="faction_xenon" banner="diplomacy_banner_xenon" />
      <!-- At war with the entire galaxy. Base-game factions first, then DLC. -->
      <relations locked="1">
        <relation faction="player" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="twitchally" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="alliance" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="antigone" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="argon" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="buccaneers" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="civilian" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="criminal" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="hatikvah" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="holyorder" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="holyorderfanatic" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="khaak" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="ministry" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="outlaw" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="paranid" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="scaleplate" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="smuggler" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="teladi" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="trinity" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="visitor" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="xenon" relation="-1" />
        <!-- Kingdom End -->
        <relation faction="boron" relation="-1" />
        <!-- Cradle of Humanity -->
        <relation faction="terran" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="pioneers" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="yaki" relation="-1" />
        <!-- Split Vendetta -->
        <relation faction="split" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="freesplit" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="fallensplit" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="court" relation="-1" />
        <!-- Tides of Avarice -->
        <relation faction="loanshark" relation="-1" />
        <relation faction="scavenger" relation="-1" />
        <!-- Timelines -->
        <relation faction="kaori" relation="-1" />
      </relations>
      <signals>
        <response signal="policehalt" response="attack" />
      </signals>
    </faction>
  </add>
</diff>
